In order to investigate the possible CME/LPV effect, we study the difference between \(UD\) and \(LR\) asymmetry correlations of the variance (\(\Delta\langle A^{2}\rangle=\delta\langle A_{UD}^{2}\rangle-\delta\langle A_{LR }^{2}\rangle\)) and covariance (\(\Delta\langle A_{+}A_{-}\rangle=\langle A_{+}A_{-}\rangle_{UD}-\langle A_{+} A_{-}\rangle_{LR}\)). The charge independent background not related to event-plane cancels by taking the difference. For variances, we take the difference between the dynamical correlations, where statistical fluctuation and detector effects have been subtracted according to different charges and \(\eta\) regions respectively.

