VITA

Quan Wang was born in Shanhaiguan, China on February 22nd, 1979. He received his Bachelar of Science Degree in Physics in May 2002 from University of Science and Technology of China (USTC). He received his Master of Science Degree from USTC in experimental particle physics in Physics from USTC in December 2005. The thesis title is "Magnetic Spectrometer for Thermal Particles in Sub-picosecond Pulse". He served as graduate student teaching assistant and research assistant at USTC during 2002-2005. He received his Ph.D. in experimental high energy nuclear physics from Purdue University in May 2012 and hired as graduate student teaching assistant in 2005-2007, and reasearch assistent in 2007-2012. In the thesis, he used correlation method to give further insight of the charge separation effect in relativistic heavy ion collisions, which suggests a flow related background. The thesis title is "Charge Multiplicity Asymmetry Correlation Study Searching for Local Parity Violation At RHIC For STAR Collaboration".